@startuml
state program #pink
program : on chain account program

state wallet #yellow
wallet : reader's wallet, on whatever device it is

state screen #cyan
screen : visible or interactive content

state server
server : site's server, no signature

state identified <<choice>>
state prove_key
state set_meter #cyan
state scan #yellow
state setup #pink
state continue #cyan
state metered_page #cyan
state meter_and_settle #pink
state check_limit <<choice>>
state manage_meter #cyan
state close_meter #pink

[*] -[bold]-> identified : navigate
identified --> set_meter : no meter known for this browser
identified -[bold]-> prove_key : meter address known

prove_key : fetch the meter at [meter, site, fund]
prove_key : page signs the server's nonce with its browser key
prove_key : verify_key against the key the meter names
prove_key : check meter key, expiry and site
prove_key -> set_meter : no meter, or the proof fails
prove_key -[bold]-> check_limit : live meter

set_meter : inform cost per item
set_meter : prompt deposit, limit and which fund
set_meter : enforce minimum on limit amount
set_meter : page generates its browser key, posts the public half
set_meter : reused for the first setting, a renewal and a new device
set_meter --> scan : show the Solana Pay link

scan : wallet fetches the transaction from the site's server
scan : reader reads it and signs, in the wallet
scan -> set_meter : reader declines
scan --> setup : wallet submits

setup : open_fund, if the named fund is new
setup : deposit, if the reader chose an amount
setup : open_meter or renew_meter, naming key, limit and expiry
setup : one transaction, signed and paid for by the reader
setup --> continue

continue : reader returns and clicks continue
continue : server fetches the meter once; nothing polls
continue -> continue : not landed yet
continue --> check_limit : meter found

check_limit -> manage_meter : limit reached, or past expiry
check_limit -[bold]-> meter_and_settle : live and below limit

meter_and_settle : refuse past the expiry
meter_and_settle : bump used amount on account by item increment
meter_and_settle : if unpaid balance crosses collection threshold,
meter_and_settle : transfer the entire unpaid balance from the fund
meter_and_settle : increment and transfer succeed or fail together (atomic)
meter_and_settle -[bold]-> metered_page : instruction succeeded
meter_and_settle --> manage_meter : instruction failed (fund short, expired)

metered_page : display metered content as navigated
metered_page -[bold]-> [*] : navigate

manage_meter : show limit, cost per item, used and paid, expiry
manage_meter : show the fund's balance, and any shortfall
manage_meter : prompt a new limit, or a deposit
manage_meter -> [*] : navigate
manage_meter --> set_meter : renew or extend
manage_meter --> close_meter : sign out

close_meter : signed by the browser key; the server pays the fee
close_meter : residue is always below the collection threshold,
close_meter : so it is left uncollected (the site takes the loss)
close_meter : rent returns to the reader
close_meter --> [*] : navigate

legend left
Colour says what kind of step it is, not who runs it.
The pink (on chain) steps divide by signer:
  reader's wallet signs ... open_fund, deposit, open_meter, renew_meter
  browser key signs ....... close_meter, and the key proof off chain
  site authority signs .... meter_and_settle
Withdrawing from a fund and closing it are the reader's too, on a
management page of their own, and appear nowhere in a site's flow.
See wasm-client/SPEC.md sections 4.7 to 4.9.
endlegend

@enduml
